    "note": "candidate-005 — addresses the Make render error (\"Failed initializing scaling graph: Resource temporarily unavailable\") on the heavy 20-point case. You're right that it's desktop/app-side: the m0 is valid and renders fine in the canonical CLI path (verified, both light & dark), but Make's executor expands each tile to its own ffmpeg scaling pass (~151 units for this doc) and exhausted a system resource (EAGAIN). The template was emitting one tile PER mark — 20 points = 40 separate marker tiles + line + area + grid + labels (~63 tiles). FIX: draw every same-color mark group as ONE multi-subpath mask — all halos = 1 tile, all dots = 1 tile, all gridlines = 1 tile, axis = 1 tile. Tile count is now FLAT as data grows: this 20-point case dropped 63 → 21 tiles (same as the 8-point default); a 30-point series is ~13. Verified visually identical (CLI renders, light + dark) and across 14 edge cases. The lighter doc should stay under Make's resource limit. (If Make STILL errors at this tile count, it's a confirmed core/executor robustness bug — it should cap concurrency / retry on EAGAIN — and I'll write it up as a separate core issue, independent of this template.)",
